# PAWai environment variables — copy to .env.local and fill in.
# Every variable below is optional-by-design: with none of them set the app
# still builds and runs (device-local record, no email). Each one switches on
# exactly one capability.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Persistent record storage (Phase 0)
# Postgres connection string — Neon / Vercel Postgres / Supabase / local all
# work. Use the *pooled* connection string on serverless hosts.
# The schema self-provisions on first use (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS) —
# there is no migration step to run.
# Switches on: durable records, /record/<token> pages, POST /api/record,
# and the private record link in the summary email + intake response.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host/db?sslmode=require

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transactional email (Phase 0)
# Resend API key — https://resend.com. When set, /api/intake sends the
# user-facing summary email itself instead of relying on n8n → Gmail.
# NOTE: while this is live AND the n8n Gmail credential works, disable the
# visitor-email node in the n8n workflow so visitors don't get two emails
# (keep the sheet/admin branch on).
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...

# Sender address. Without it, PAWai <onboarding@resend.dev> is used, which
# only delivers to the Resend account owner — fine for testing, useless for
# real visitors. For production, verify a domain in Resend and use it here.
# RESEND_FROM=PAWai <care@pawai.it.com>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Passwordless sign-in (Phase 0)
# No new env var: reuses DATABASE_URL (sessions table) and RESEND_API_KEY
# (login-link email) above — both must be set for /signin to work.
# Switches on: POST /api/auth/request, the /signin/verify confirmation page
# (whose form POSTs to /api/auth/verify), and the /signin page.
# Sign-in links are throttled per email (3 per 15 min, 10 per 24 h).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application origin for server-minted links (magic-link emails, Care Card
# record links). NOT for SEO surfaces — sitemap/metadata keep the canonical
# SITE_URL constant. Resolution: APP_ORIGIN if set (validated http(s) URL) →
# http://localhost:<PORT|3000> outside production → https://pawai.it.com in
# production. Set this on preview/staging deploys so emailed links point at
# the environment that generated them.
# APP_ORIGIN=https://pawai.it.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backup & security notes (operational, not code)
# - Postgres backups/point-in-time recovery are the provider's job — confirm
#   the plan tier (Neon/Vercel Postgres/Supabase) actually includes PITR;
#   PAWai's own code does not run backups.
# - Session + record tokens are 192-bit random (crypto.randomBytes) capability
#   URLs/cookies — treat a leaked token as a leaked login, there is no second
#   factor. The session cookie is httpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax.
# - Turn on 2FA on the Neon, Resend, and Vercel account dashboards themselves
#   — that is account-level and outside anything this codebase can enforce.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Existing n8n pipeline (sheet row + admin notification; also the visitor
# email while Resend is not configured)
# N8N_WEBHOOK_URL=https://...
# N8N_API_KEY=...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ElevenLabs voice agents (existing)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ELEVENLABS_HEALTH_AGENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ELEVENLABS_BEHAVIOR_AGENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ELEVENLABS_NEW_PET_AGENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ELEVENLABS_SUPPORT_AGENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ELEVENLABS_CARE_AGENT_ID=
